1
00:00:10,327 --> 00:00:12,109
Listen to one sound near you.

2
00:00:12,189 --> 00:00:16,040
A car going by, or a fan.
Now ask: what made it?

3
00:00:16,849 --> 00:00:21,963
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:22,781 --> 00:00:26,682
Dependent arising runs through
almost everything I write.

5
00:00:26,762 --> 00:00:28,951
The eight steps of the logic use it.

6
00:00:29,031 --> 00:00:33,774
So do the pages on cause and
effect, on continuity, and on mind.

7
00:00:33,854 --> 00:00:35,853
Each uses it for its own question.

8
00:00:35,933 --> 00:00:39,127
None of them sets out
the view itself, whole,

9
00:00:39,207 --> 00:00:42,026
and says what it is for. This one does.

10
00:00:42,862 --> 00:00:48,828
That matters, because dependent arising is
easy to agree with, and easy to mishear.

11
00:00:48,908 --> 00:00:52,538
Most people already accept that
things depend on other things.

12
00:00:52,618 --> 00:00:54,539
Then they hear one of five things.

13
00:00:55,357 --> 00:00:59,964
A web: things are unfindable, but
surely the connections are there,

14
00:01:00,044 --> 00:01:04,000
a network, a field of
relations, the floor at last.

15
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:08,375
A machine: causes working in
the dark, each pushing the next.

16
00:01:08,455 --> 00:01:12,233
Only concepts: if it is
designated, it is a story,

17
00:01:12,313 --> 00:01:14,421
and causes are not really there.

18
00:01:14,501 --> 00:01:19,421
A lower truth: fine for the world,
to be left behind at the ultimate.

19
00:01:19,501 --> 00:01:23,986
And the shape of ignorance: the
twelve links begin with ignorance,

20
00:01:24,066 --> 00:01:27,700
so dependent arising must
be the pattern of confusion.

21
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:31,731
Each takes something true and
sets it on the wrong foot.

22
00:01:32,541 --> 00:01:34,096
Start with what it says.

23
00:01:35,113 --> 00:01:37,098
A bell rings when it is struck.

24
00:01:37,178 --> 00:01:39,109
A seed of rice gives rice.

25
00:01:39,189 --> 00:01:43,226
A harsh word, met with a
certain mood, brings anger.

26
00:01:43,306 --> 00:01:46,731
The order is reliable,
and actions have results.

27
00:01:46,811 --> 00:01:50,196
Dependent arising says: these conditions,

28
00:01:50,276 --> 00:01:52,736
met together, and this appears.

29
00:01:52,816 --> 00:01:54,534
Designated, and working.

30
00:01:55,362 --> 00:01:59,046
What it never says is that a
cause, standing on its own,

31
00:01:59,126 --> 00:02:01,804
makes an effect and hands it across.

32
00:02:01,884 --> 00:02:05,092
The ringing is not made
by the bronze, the strike,

33
00:02:05,172 --> 00:02:09,508
the air and the ear, and then
sent out. It is their meeting.

34
00:02:09,588 --> 00:02:12,402
Nothing passes from the
strike to the sound,

35
00:02:12,482 --> 00:02:15,568
and nothing stands behind
the sound producing it.

36
00:02:15,648 --> 00:02:18,548
Yet without the strike,
there is no ringing.

37
00:02:19,366 --> 00:02:23,159
This is what I call causal
efficacy without causal power.

38
00:02:23,239 --> 00:02:25,319
Conditions condition, fully.

39
00:02:25,399 --> 00:02:28,761
And no power is ever
found sitting in a cause.

40
00:02:29,581 --> 00:02:32,707
Dependent arising did not
come to me as a theory.

41
00:02:32,787 --> 00:02:36,815
It came as the same seeing
as anatta, turned outwards.

42
00:02:37,625 --> 00:02:41,471
Anatta is the insight that
there is no doer behind seeing.

43
00:02:41,551 --> 00:02:43,577
In seeing, only the seen.

44
00:02:43,657 --> 00:02:45,710
In hearing, only the heard.

45
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,789
The person does not disappear.

46
00:02:47,869 --> 00:02:51,553
You still have a name, catch
the bus and keep your promises.

47
00:02:51,633 --> 00:02:55,955
What falls away is one picture:
someone standing behind the action,

48
00:02:56,035 --> 00:02:57,235
making it happen.

49
00:02:57,981 --> 00:03:01,162
Nāgārjuna makes the same move everywhere.

50
00:03:01,242 --> 00:03:03,213
There is no goer behind going.

51
00:03:03,293 --> 00:03:08,281
There is no seer behind seeing, no
fire standing apart from its fuel,

52
00:03:08,361 --> 00:03:10,482
and no producer behind arising.

53
00:03:10,562 --> 00:03:14,599
Dependent arising is this:
no doer behind anything.

54
00:03:14,679 --> 00:03:18,906
The wind is blowing, and there is
no wind apart from the blowing.

55
00:03:18,986 --> 00:03:22,389
It is raining, and there
is no "it" that rains.

56
00:03:23,209 --> 00:03:27,273
So anatta and dependent
arising are not two subjects.

57
00:03:27,353 --> 00:03:31,390
Anatta, met first, takes
the doer out of seeing.

58
00:03:31,470 --> 00:03:34,881
Dependent arising takes
it out of everything else:

59
00:03:34,961 --> 00:03:38,772
the cause, the object,
the whole, the field.

60
00:03:39,581 --> 00:03:44,324
Now designation. It is not a second
teaching beside dependent arising.

61
00:03:44,404 --> 00:03:47,929
It is the same seeing,
turned on the "this" itself.

62
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:51,040
Designation does not need words.

63
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:53,146
It needs only singling out.

64
00:03:53,226 --> 00:03:57,593
This sound, this colour, this
ache, picked out as "this".

65
00:03:57,764 --> 00:04:01,040
A "this" stands out only
against what it is not,

66
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:03,119
and only with these conditions.

67
00:04:03,199 --> 00:04:06,556
In a world of only blue,
no one would see blue.

68
00:04:06,636 --> 00:04:10,415
So the singling out is not done to
an appearance that was there first,

69
00:04:10,495 --> 00:04:13,214
waiting to be named. It is the appearing.

70
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:16,937
And because it is already
dependence, it is already empty.

71
00:04:17,017 --> 00:04:20,419
By appearing, a thing is already empty.

72
00:04:21,242 --> 00:04:23,540
The clearest case is the oldest.

73
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:27,874
The monk Nāgasena asks King
Milinda where his chariot is.

74
00:04:27,954 --> 00:04:31,611
It is not the pole, not
the axle, not the wheels,

75
00:04:31,691 --> 00:04:35,823
not the frame, not their sum, and
not something apart from them.

76
00:04:35,903 --> 00:04:40,170
Candrakīrti makes the search
complete, in seven ways.

77
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:42,997
The chariot is not the same as its parts,

78
00:04:43,077 --> 00:04:45,841
not other than them,
does not possess them,

79
00:04:45,943 --> 00:04:50,021
is not in them, does not contain
them, is not their collection,

80
00:04:50,101 --> 00:04:52,906
and is not their shape. Nothing is found.

81
00:04:53,705 --> 00:04:55,853
Yet the chariot is not denied.

82
00:04:55,933 --> 00:04:57,674
It still carries you to town.

83
00:04:57,754 --> 00:05:01,546
It is set up by designation,
in dependence on its parts,

84
00:05:01,626 --> 00:05:04,983
and the world's way of
speaking of it is left intact.

85
00:05:05,063 --> 00:05:10,350
For me, the chariot was never only
about chariots. Walking is the chariot.

86
00:05:10,430 --> 00:05:12,067
Hearing is the chariot.

87
00:05:12,885 --> 00:05:14,897
And the parts are designated too.

88
00:05:14,977 --> 00:05:17,696
The chariot is designated on its wheels.

89
00:05:17,776 --> 00:05:22,071
But a wheel is singled out in
turn, on rim, spokes and hub.

90
00:05:22,151 --> 00:05:24,992
And they on their wood.
And the wood on its grain.

91
00:05:25,072 --> 00:05:30,196
No bottom layer is ever reached, where
something finally stands by itself and

92
00:05:30,276 --> 00:05:32,017
receives the first name.

93
00:05:32,097 --> 00:05:36,872
Not because the search was cut short, but
because there is nowhere for it to end.

94
00:05:37,762 --> 00:05:41,065
"Merely designated" does
not mean "only a name".

95
00:05:41,145 --> 00:05:44,218
Designation and
functioning arise together.

96
00:05:44,298 --> 00:05:47,234
The chariot is called a
chariot because it carries.

97
00:05:47,314 --> 00:05:51,908
A designation holds because it works
within its agreements and its setting.

98
00:05:51,988 --> 00:05:55,807
And the mind that seems to do the
designating is singled out too.

99
00:05:55,887 --> 00:05:58,393
No one stands behind it, doing it.

100
00:05:59,213 --> 00:06:02,683
Once the things are seen
through, two pictures creep back.

101
00:06:03,502 --> 00:06:05,773
The first puts the conditions underneath,

102
00:06:05,853 --> 00:06:09,985
as parts lined up below that then
produce the appearing on top.

103
00:06:10,065 --> 00:06:14,210
But the conditions are the appearing,
cut into parts by a framework,

104
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:17,009
for explaining and for
getting things done.

105
00:06:17,089 --> 00:06:21,316
The cook, the chemist and the physicist
cut the same loaf differently,

106
00:06:21,396 --> 00:06:23,015
and each cut works.

107
00:06:23,095 --> 00:06:25,655
None of them is the
loaf from its own side.

108
00:06:26,474 --> 00:06:29,601
The second keeps the relations
when the things are gone:

109
00:06:29,681 --> 00:06:32,277
a web, a network, a field.

110
00:06:32,357 --> 00:06:35,076
But the line is as unfindable as the dot.

111
00:06:35,156 --> 00:06:39,057
Nāgārjuna says it plainly:
coming into contact,

112
00:06:39,137 --> 00:06:43,935
what has come into contact, and the one
who brings them together are not found.

113
00:06:44,015 --> 00:06:48,989
Relation and what is related are
designated together. Neither comes first.

114
00:06:49,069 --> 00:06:54,248
Indra's net is a fine image, so long as
the net itself is not taken as what is

115
00:06:54,328 --> 00:06:55,665
finally found.

116
00:06:56,465 --> 00:06:59,754
So "nothing stands alone"
is only half of it.

117
00:06:59,834 --> 00:07:04,550
The other half is that the relations are
not found from their own side either.

118
00:07:04,630 --> 00:07:06,276
What is left is not a web.

119
00:07:06,356 --> 00:07:08,047
It is this, appearing.

120
00:07:08,853 --> 00:07:11,449
There are two ways of
knowing rightly here,

121
00:07:11,529 --> 00:07:13,492
and it helps not to collapse them.

122
00:07:14,318 --> 00:07:17,852
The first works through
concepts, within the framework.

123
00:07:17,932 --> 00:07:21,181
Dependent arising is how
the whole net comes about.

124
00:07:21,261 --> 00:07:26,956
The net is conventional and empty, and it
keeps presenting itself upon conditions,

125
00:07:27,036 --> 00:07:28,776
for functional purposes.

126
00:07:28,856 --> 00:07:30,488
This is not a lesser knowing.

127
00:07:30,568 --> 00:07:34,021
It is how a doctor
treats, how a cook cooks,

128
00:07:34,101 --> 00:07:37,920
how a promise is kept,
how karma is understood.

129
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:42,146
And in this mode, dependent
arising also shows emptiness,

130
00:07:42,226 --> 00:07:45,900
and corrects the inherent reading
from inside the framework.

131
00:07:46,722 --> 00:07:49,862
The second is freedom
from all elaborations.

132
00:07:49,942 --> 00:07:52,036
It is not within the framework at all.

133
00:07:52,116 --> 00:07:57,525
Nothing is cut into before and after,
part and whole, cause and effect.

134
00:07:57,605 --> 00:08:00,872
Without the framework, there
is one complete stroke.

135
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:03,389
Neither cancels the other.

136
00:08:03,469 --> 00:08:05,821
The first is not a ladder to throw away.

137
00:08:05,901 --> 00:08:09,494
The second is not a place
outside the world to retreat to.

138
00:08:09,623 --> 00:08:13,538
Freedom kept apart from the
framework would become a new ground.

139
00:08:13,618 --> 00:08:17,560
So after it, the taste is met
again inside the framework,

140
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:21,627
in ordinary life, with the
parts and conditions now light.

141
00:08:22,442 --> 00:08:26,742
Within the framework, dependent
arising does three kinds of work.

142
00:08:27,545 --> 00:08:31,690
It explains. It answers the
question, how does this come about?

143
00:08:31,770 --> 00:08:34,004
These conditions, met together.

144
00:08:34,821 --> 00:08:36,113
It dismantles.

145
00:08:36,193 --> 00:08:40,610
Because a thing arises in dependence,
it is not there from its own side.

146
00:08:40,690 --> 00:08:44,129
So dependence is the reason
that takes apart the self,

147
00:08:44,209 --> 00:08:48,070
the object, the cause,
the whole, the field,

148
00:08:48,150 --> 00:08:52,553
the substrate, energy and
the web. It shows emptiness.

149
00:08:52,633 --> 00:08:56,498
Tsongkhapa's tradition calls
it the king of reasons.

150
00:08:57,313 --> 00:08:59,026
And it describes the taste.

151
00:08:59,106 --> 00:09:03,850
Seen through, it is the taste
itself: nothing standing on its own,

152
00:09:03,930 --> 00:09:05,130
nothing missing.

153
00:09:05,922 --> 00:09:09,647
They hang together. It can
dismantle because it explains.

154
00:09:09,727 --> 00:09:13,111
What validly depends cannot
also stand by itself.

155
00:09:13,191 --> 00:09:16,562
So the reasoning does not
destroy the world it takes apart.

156
00:09:16,642 --> 00:09:19,212
What goes is only the "from its own side".

157
00:09:19,292 --> 00:09:22,011
And it puts nothing in
place of what it removes.

158
00:09:22,091 --> 00:09:27,681
It dismantles itself too, since dependence
is not found from its own side either.

159
00:09:28,497 --> 00:09:31,256
Dependent arising is an enlightened view.

160
00:09:31,336 --> 00:09:35,047
By that I do not mean a view that
only the enlightened can hold.

161
00:09:35,127 --> 00:09:39,617
I mean the right view of how things
are, which we do not yet live in.

162
00:09:40,442 --> 00:09:43,813
We do not live in the
wisdom of dependent arising.

163
00:09:43,893 --> 00:09:48,025
We live reading the matrix as
inherent, within the framework.

164
00:09:48,105 --> 00:09:51,775
Things seem to stand by
themselves. Causes seem to push.

165
00:09:51,855 --> 00:09:54,302
A self seems to sit behind the seeing.

166
00:09:54,382 --> 00:09:56,585
That seeming is not a thought we hold.

167
00:09:56,665 --> 00:10:00,978
It is a deep habit of seeing,
in the body, before thought.

168
00:10:01,793 --> 00:10:03,941
So I keep two frameworks apart.

169
00:10:04,021 --> 00:10:07,446
The default framework is the
conventional cutting itself:

170
00:10:07,526 --> 00:10:11,373
parts and whole, before and
after, cause and effect,

171
00:10:11,453 --> 00:10:13,248
set in a time sequence.

172
00:10:13,328 --> 00:10:17,976
It works, and we need it to speak,
to cook and to keep promises.

173
00:10:18,056 --> 00:10:20,232
Dependent arising lives here.

174
00:10:20,312 --> 00:10:24,525
The inherent framework is the habit of
taking what the cutting singles out as

175
00:10:24,605 --> 00:10:27,745
standing by itself. That is the matrix.

176
00:10:27,825 --> 00:10:31,242
Not a world, not a
field. A habit of seeing.

177
00:10:32,061 --> 00:10:36,695
Dependent arising lives in the
first, and unbinds the second.

178
00:10:36,775 --> 00:10:41,994
Run the two together, and "it lives in
a framework" is heard as "it is only a

179
00:10:42,074 --> 00:10:45,545
story". That is the
slide into annihilation.

180
00:10:46,358 --> 00:10:50,517
Some readings say dependent
arising originates with ignorance,

181
00:10:50,597 --> 00:10:52,773
since the twelve links begin there.

182
00:10:52,853 --> 00:10:54,607
That reading needs refining.

183
00:10:54,687 --> 00:10:59,335
Ignorance is not a power, a thing
in us with a force to blind.

184
00:10:59,415 --> 00:11:02,637
It is a very deep habit
of confused seeing,

185
00:11:02,717 --> 00:11:06,727
designated as ignorance, and
not found when searched for.

186
00:11:06,807 --> 00:11:10,844
It blinds reliably because its
conditions keep being renewed.

187
00:11:10,924 --> 00:11:14,258
And it can end, because
nothing stands behind it.

188
00:11:15,090 --> 00:11:20,296
Dependent arising, as a view, originates
as the corrective antidote for that

189
00:11:20,376 --> 00:11:21,576
ignorance.

190
00:11:22,233 --> 00:11:27,058
If it simply came from ignorance, it would
be strange to praise it as the supreme

191
00:11:27,138 --> 00:11:29,789
teaching. Yet that is what the texts do.

192
00:11:29,869 --> 00:11:35,590
Nāgārjuna opens his verses by bowing to
the Buddha who taught dependent arising:

193
00:11:35,670 --> 00:11:41,079
without arising or ceasing, the
stilling of elaborations, peace.

194
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:46,908
Tsongkhapa wrote a whole praise to it, and
said that seeing it reverses ignorance,

195
00:11:46,988 --> 00:11:49,843
the root of the round of birth and death.

196
00:11:49,923 --> 00:11:54,793
And the Buddha said: whoever sees
dependent arising sees the Dhamma.

197
00:11:55,610 --> 00:11:58,112
The twelve links do begin with ignorance,

198
00:11:58,192 --> 00:12:00,082
and no master denies it.

199
00:12:00,162 --> 00:12:04,022
In forward order, they show how
the round of suffering runs.

200
00:12:04,102 --> 00:12:06,862
In reverse order, they show how it ends.

201
00:12:06,942 --> 00:12:10,299
What is praised is dependent
arising seen rightly,

202
00:12:10,379 --> 00:12:12,691
and that seeing is the antidote.

203
00:12:12,771 --> 00:12:14,634
No one praises ignorance.

204
00:12:14,714 --> 00:12:17,002
They praise the seeing that undoes it.

205
00:12:17,801 --> 00:12:21,579
I have read more than once that
conventional truth is a veil.

206
00:12:21,659 --> 00:12:27,585
So dependent arising, being conventional,
must be the veil. The source is genuine.

207
00:12:27,665 --> 00:12:32,299
The Sanskrit word for conventional,
saṃvṛti, can mean a covering.

208
00:12:32,379 --> 00:12:35,791
But Candrakīrti gives
the word three meanings:

209
00:12:35,871 --> 00:12:39,532
concealment, the ignorance
that hides how things are;

210
00:12:39,621 --> 00:12:42,626
mutual dependence; and worldly convention,

211
00:12:42,706 --> 00:12:45,184
the names by which the world speaks.

212
00:12:46,005 --> 00:12:49,050
Read carefully, this
supports the refinement.

213
00:12:49,130 --> 00:12:51,944
What veils is ignorance, the concealer.

214
00:12:52,024 --> 00:12:55,694
Dependent arising is the second
meaning of the same word.

215
00:12:55,774 --> 00:12:58,275
The same appearance can be held two ways.

216
00:12:58,355 --> 00:13:01,889
Held by the concealer, it
seems to stand by itself,

217
00:13:01,969 --> 00:13:04,036
and that seeming is the veil.

218
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:08,701
Seen as dependent arising, it is
the seeing that lifts the veil.

219
00:13:09,505 --> 00:13:12,292
Candrakīrti says as much himself.

220
00:13:12,372 --> 00:13:14,778
For those who have let
go of that ignorance,

221
00:13:14,858 --> 00:13:17,047
things appear like reflections.

222
00:13:17,127 --> 00:13:21,368
Still appearing, still working,
no longer taken as true.

223
00:13:21,448 --> 00:13:23,120
He calls this mere convention.

224
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:26,898
The conventional, read
with ignorance, veils.

225
00:13:26,978 --> 00:13:29,035
With wisdom, why would it veil?

226
00:13:29,837 --> 00:13:32,791
And here is how it meets
spontaneous presence.

227
00:13:33,609 --> 00:13:38,203
Dependent arising is how the appearing
is described when we analyse:

228
00:13:38,283 --> 00:13:42,537
these conditions, met
together, designated, working.

229
00:13:42,617 --> 00:13:47,578
Spontaneous presence is how it is
described when the habit of fixing stops:

230
00:13:47,658 --> 00:13:52,799
complete, effortless, with nothing
behind it. They are not two things.

231
00:13:53,605 --> 00:13:55,318
Keep two questions apart.

232
00:13:55,398 --> 00:13:57,315
How does this appearing come about?

233
00:13:57,395 --> 00:14:03,395
Through causes and conditions, always.
What is its nature? Empty. Not produced.

234
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:08,593
Dzogchen says spontaneous presence
is not made by causes and conditions.

235
00:14:08,673 --> 00:14:12,302
I read that as Nāgārjuna's
"without arising":

236
00:14:12,382 --> 00:14:16,776
appearing through conditions, yet
with no birth from its own side.

237
00:14:17,585 --> 00:14:21,717
Neither description is higher,
and one does not become the other,

238
00:14:21,797 --> 00:14:24,122
any more than summer becomes winter.

239
00:14:24,202 --> 00:14:29,244
Dependent arising keeps spontaneous
presence from being heard as coming from a

240
00:14:29,324 --> 00:14:30,507
hidden ground.

241
00:14:30,587 --> 00:14:36,069
Spontaneous presence keeps dependent
arising from being heard as a mechanism.

242
00:14:36,885 --> 00:14:40,813
At the core, I do not think this
departs from the orthodox view.

243
00:14:40,893 --> 00:14:46,850
It is the Prāsaṅgika reading of Nāgārjuna
as Candrakīrti and Tsongkhapa give it:

244
00:14:46,993 --> 00:14:49,644
reasoning refutes production
by its own nature,

245
00:14:49,724 --> 00:14:52,353
not production as the world speaks of it.

246
00:14:53,174 --> 00:14:57,198
Where I may part from how some
masters are read is in four places.

247
00:14:57,278 --> 00:15:01,740
Its status: I hold dependent
arising as an enlightened view,

248
00:15:01,843 --> 00:15:05,241
not only a description of
the world to be left behind.

249
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:10,227
Its origin: I read it as the antidote
by which ignorance is undone,

250
00:15:10,307 --> 00:15:12,442
not as the pattern of ignorance.

251
00:15:12,522 --> 00:15:17,524
Its object: nothing stands alone, but
the relations are not found either,

252
00:15:17,604 --> 00:15:19,915
so I do not make the net the real.

253
00:15:19,995 --> 00:15:24,181
And bridges: I do not need a link
to carry an act to its fruit.

254
00:15:24,261 --> 00:15:28,126
These are my readings, not the
schools'. Weigh both sides.

255
00:15:28,979 --> 00:15:30,724
Five guards, to end.

256
00:15:31,521 --> 00:15:37,521
Not only concepts. Designated does not
mean unreal or arbitrary. Things work.

257
00:15:37,744 --> 00:15:40,385
Harm is harm. Actions bear fruit.

258
00:15:41,197 --> 00:15:44,663
Not uncaused. Every
appearing has its conditions.

259
00:15:44,743 --> 00:15:47,493
What is gone is the
producer, not the order.

260
00:15:48,305 --> 00:15:50,385
Not a web, and not a ground.

261
00:15:50,465 --> 00:15:53,483
The relations are no more
found than the things.

262
00:15:53,563 --> 00:15:55,539
Emptiness is not a new something.

263
00:15:56,349 --> 00:15:58,320
Not a stage to leave behind.

264
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:01,717
The framework is not the
prison. Reifying it is.

265
00:16:01,797 --> 00:16:06,178
Dependent arising is held,
lightly, in ordinary life.

266
00:16:06,985 --> 00:16:11,538
And not a state to keep. Seeing
dependence is not maintained by effort.

267
00:16:11,618 --> 00:16:13,372
Maintenance is the split.

268
00:16:13,452 --> 00:16:16,705
It is seen, and in time the habit loosens.

269
00:16:17,525 --> 00:16:21,417
Try it. Take that sound
again, the car or the fan.

270
00:16:21,533 --> 00:16:24,727
Find its conditions: the source, the air,

271
00:16:24,807 --> 00:16:26,548
the ear, attention.

272
00:16:26,628 --> 00:16:30,506
The sound is not made by them and
sent out. It is their meeting.

273
00:16:31,329 --> 00:16:35,162
Change one condition. Cover
one ear, or turn your head.

274
00:16:35,242 --> 00:16:38,903
It is not the same sound altered.
It is a different appearing.

275
00:16:39,695 --> 00:16:41,313
Look for whoever is hearing.

276
00:16:41,393 --> 00:16:44,778
Then look for the "between"
that joins the conditions.

277
00:16:44,858 --> 00:16:47,133
Can either be found
apart from the hearing?

278
00:16:47,945 --> 00:16:51,248
Then ask: did any of this
need a hearer behind it,

279
00:16:51,328 --> 00:16:54,414
a web underneath, or a power in the cause?

280
00:16:54,494 --> 00:16:57,108
Let the question go, and hear the sound.

